      "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.677,
      "end": 16.097,
      "text": "Unfortunately lavender usually doesn't regrow from old bare wood. If you cut into it, those stems often stay bare."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 18.627,
      "end": 24.357,
      "text": "It is. The good news is lavender is cheap and easy to replace, and you can take cuttings from the green tips first."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 27.537,
      "end": 33.817,
      "text": "Trim them every year right after flowering, taking off the flower stalks and a bit of the green. Never go into the brown."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 43.167,
      "end": 48.077,
      "text": "Then it did really well to last that long. Start fresh and give the new ones a trim every August."
    }
